From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] shared-qmi: don't assert when the LOC inject-request handlers
 are already connected

loc_register_event_inject_req_ready() asserts that the two
inject-{time,position}-request handler ids are unset before connecting them.
But `priv` is per-modem-object qdata (get_private()) and those ids are only
ever cleared in dispose(). The Location interface can be initialized more than
once on the same modem object -- unlocking the SIM PIN takes the modem
locked -> initializing, which is a second pass -- and the assertion then aborts
the daemon:

  ModemManager: Bail out! ERROR:../src/mm-shared-qmi.c:7061:
    loc_register_event_inject_req_ready: assertion failed:
    (!priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id)
  ModemManager.service: Failed with result 'core-dump'.

To the user the modem appears to crash: ModemManager dies, the modem vanishes
from the desktop's network settings and any active bearer drops. The modem
firmware is fine -- on the affected device the MSS remoteproc stays running
throughout.

Reproduced on demand three times on a Qualcomm MSM8998 (Google Pixel 2 XL),
under both GNOME and phosh, simply by running `mmcli -i any --pin=****`.

Disconnect any handler left over from a previous initialization instead of
asserting. priv->loc_client is used as the instance, matching what dispose()
already does, which also covers the case where re-initialization handed us a
fresh QmiClientLoc.

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/src/mm-shared-qmi.c
+++ b/src/mm-shared-qmi.c
@@ -7058,14 +7058,27 @@
     self = g_task_get_source_object (task);
     priv = get_private (self);
 
-    g_assert (!priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id);
+    /* The Location interface can be initialized more than once on the same
+     * modem object -- a SIM lock state change is enough -- and these ids are
+     * only cleared in dispose(), so they may still be set from a previous
+     * pass. Drop the stale handlers instead of asserting; the client may be a
+     * different one this time round, so disconnect from the stored one. */
+    if (priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id) {
+        g_signal_handler_disconnect (priv->loc_client,
+                                     priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id);
+        priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id = 0;
+    }
     priv->loc_assistance_inject_time_req_indication_id =
         g_signal_connect (client,
                           "inject-time-request",
                           G_CALLBACK (loc_location_inject_time_req_indication_cb),
                           self);
 
-    g_assert (!priv->loc_assistance_inject_position_req_indication_id);
+    if (priv->loc_assistance_inject_position_req_indication_id) {
+        g_signal_handler_disconnect (priv->loc_client,
+                                     priv->loc_assistance_inject_position_req_indication_id);
+        priv->loc_assistance_inject_position_req_indication_id = 0;
+    }
     priv->loc_assistance_inject_position_req_indication_id =
         g_signal_connect (client,
                           "inject-position-request",
